{
 "issues": [
  {
   "analyst": "S1",
   "problem": "The code computes delay as the difference between timestamps on the same date and never adjusts post-midnight actual departures. Thus an actual departure after midnight is treated as roughly 1,440 minutes early rather than as a delayed departure, despite the notes claiming overnight departures were handled."
  },
  {
   "analyst": "S3",
   "problem": "Likewise, the code never adjusts negative timestamp differences for post-midnight actual departures. Its reported rates therefore misclassify overnight departures and cannot support the stated result."
  },
  {
   "analyst": "S2",
   "problem": "The `delay2` correction adds 1,440 minutes to every negative delay. That is only valid for an actual departure after midnight; a genuinely early same-day departure should remain negative. The code needs an explicit overnight criterion rather than converting all negative values."
  },
  {
   "analyst": "S1",
   "problem": "The submissions do not show deduplication despite the documentation warning that the export may contain repeated records. Counts should be based on unique flight_id records, if duplicates are present."
  },
