  }
 ],
 "disagreements": "S1 and S3 report substantially lower rates because their code fails to handle post-midnight actual departures. S2 reports higher rates using its second `delay2` calculation, which is closer to the documented definition, but its blanket conversion of every negative delay is not fully valid. The analysts also report different bad-weather/other group results, likely because of the delay-treatment difference (and potentially duplicate handling).",
 "best": "S2",
 "correction": "Use local scheduled date/hour to join origin weather, classify bad weather exactly as documented, exclude cancellations, and compute actual minus scheduled departure using a date adjustment only when the actual clock time is demonstrably on the following day. Deduplicate repeated flight records by flight_id before aggregation. Recalculate the two percentages and round to one decimal; S1 and S3's reported values should not be used, and S2's values are supported only if its negative-delay cases are confirmed to be the documented overnight departures rather than early same-day departures."
}
